<section class="three-tool-knowledge" id="age-guide-guide" aria-labelledby="age-guide-heading">
<h2 id="age-guide-heading">Islamic Age Calculator: complete Hijri lunar age and birthday guide</h2>
<p><strong>Short answer:</strong> Islamic age is often expressed as the number of <strong>completed Hijri lunar years</strong> since a birth date. Because a lunar year lasts roughly <strong>354–355 days</strong>, it is shorter than a Gregorian solar year and a person's numeric Hijri age is often greater. This calculator uses the named Umm al-Qura system and compares it with conventional Gregorian birthdays.</p>
